vulkan-systems | WIP

Reusable independent C++17 Vulkan and CPU modules:

  gpu/        VulkanGPU     GPU memory, descriptors, compute and barriers
  render/     VulkanRender  Frame submission, swapchain rendering, pipelines
  bvh/        VulkanBVH     GPU BLAS/TLAS and ray-query infrastructure
  lumen/      VulkanLumen   Lumen-style GI API skeleton (no rendering yet)
  spatial/    VulkanSpatial CPU index / spatial queries
  network/    VulkanNetwork Authenticated UDP / DTLS session
  jobs/       VulkanJobs    CPU job scheduling

There is deliberately NO root build.c or combined VulkanSystems target.
Each module has its own <module>/build.c, with precisely scoped sources,
include paths and dependencies. Applications fetch only the needed modules:

  C_Dependency* render=c_git(b,"VulkanRender",
    "https://github.com/xt9y/vulkan-systems.git","main");
  c_dep_subdir(render,"render");
  c_dep_cbuild(render,"VulkanRender",C_TARGET_STATIC_LIBRARY);
  c_dep_include(render,".");

For render clients, also link VulkanGPU because the render/postprocess module
uses GPU-managed images. Link users before providers (render, gpu, engine).
For a Lumen harness, additionally fetch the lumen subdirectory and link
VulkanLumen; it currently exports no-op create/set_scene/set_gbuffer/
set_lighting/invalidate/resize/record/compose/result/reset entry points.
The modules' VulkanWrapper dependencies are defined by their own build.c files.

No game-specific scene serialization, weapons, networking policy, or world
authority belongs in VulkanGPU, VulkanRender, VulkanBVH, or VulkanLumen.

The shader algorithms needed for Lumen (screen tracing, surface cache, probe
gather, world radiance cache, reflections and composite) have intentionally
NOT been implemented. See lumen/readme for the fixed integration contract.
